# core.autocrlf=input stores LF and does NOT restore CRLF on checkout, so without
# this every committed .bat/.cmd came back LF-only. cmd.exe seeks by byte offset
# while parsing, and on an LF-only file that offset drifts: comment fragments get
# executed as commands and parenthesized blocks lose their structure.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
